    "GET /api/v1/auth/callback": {"access":"Anonymous","token_policy":"Denied","scope":null,"operation":{
      "parameters":[{"name":"state","in":"query","required":true,"description":"The one-use login state: exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters (identity.rs is_token); anything else is refused 400 before any database access.","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9a-f]{64}$"}},{"name":"code","in":"query","required":true,"description":"The authorization code. A callback without a non-empty code of at most 8192 bytes is refused 400 (after consuming the attempt), so only a request carrying one can succeed.","schema":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":8192}},{"name":"error","in":"query","description":"The provider's refusal text. The handler consumes the login attempt and answers 400 to ANY request carrying it, whatever the other parameters.","x-omg-unobserved-parameter":"The provider's refusal report: identity.rs callback consumes the one-use attempt and returns 400 for any request that carries `error` (before looking at `code`), so no positive 303 response can ever carry it. A real provider sends it when the user declines sign-in; the test cannot make a successful sign-in carry it.","schema":{"type":"string"}}],
      "description":"One-use PKCE/OIDC callback. Unknown query keys are ignored. Browser refusals may redirect to sign-in without creating a session.",
